<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  UDFPS enrollment screen geometry for the A30s (SM-A307F).

  The physical sensor is sensor_location = 360|1350|119, i.e. a 238 px square
  on the 720x1560 panel (radius 119 px).

  WHAT IS WRONG BY DEFAULT, measured from source:

  1) config_udfpsEnrollProgressBar = 280 (res/values/config.xml:787), and
     UdfpsEnrollView.java:119 does

         mProgressBarRadius = scaleFactor * getInteger(config_udfpsEnrollProgressBar)

     while getPaddingX()/getPaddingY() (lines 226-231) both return that radius,
     so updateDimensions() (lines 207-208) sizes the whole UdfpsEnrollView to

         sensorBounds.width + 2 * mProgressBarRadius

     At 280 that is 238 + 560 = 798 px on a 720 px wide display - the press
     target is WIDER THAN THE SCREEN, and the progress ring it draws is 560 px
     across against a 238 px sensor.

  2) fingerprint_enroll_enrolling_base.xml:41-42 puts the RingProgressBar inside
     a FillContentLayout sized by fingerprint_progress_bar_max_size = 240dp.
     At wm density 280 that is 420 px, and RingProgressBar.onMeasure forces
     setMeasuredDimension(shortSide, shortSide), so the ring is 420x420 px.

  Both are resized here to the real sensor. 136dp x 1.75 = 238 px = the sensor
  exactly, and 68dp keeps the original 120:240 = 1:2 min:max ratio
  (68 x 1.75 = 119 px = the sensor radius).

  config_udfpsEnrollProgressBar is an integer used as a radius in px scaled by
  scaleFactor, NOT a dp dimension, hence <integer> rather than <dimen>. 119 is
  the sensor radius; if the measured scaleFactor is not 1 this must be
  119 / scaleFactor (see BUILD_NOTES.md section 25).
-->
<resources>
    <!-- v2 2026-10-03, halved at the user's request ("make button 2x smaller").
         119 was the true sensor RADIUS in px, correct for geometry but far too
         large visually. Halved to 59 px, preserving the original 1:2 min:max
         ratio:  59 x 1.75 = 103 px, and 34dp/68dp keep min:max = 1:2.
         config_udfpsEnrollProgressBar is an INTEGER used as a radius in px scaled
         by scaleFactor (NOT a dp dimension) - hence <integer>. -->
    <integer name="config_udfpsEnrollProgressBar">59</integer>
    <dimen name="fingerprint_progress_bar_max_size">68dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="fingerprint_progress_bar_min_size">34dp</dimen>
    <!-- Nudges the enrollment ring 10 px DOWN. Applied to topMargin in
         UdfpsEnrollView.updateDimensions(). Sensor rect is left truthful. -->
    <dimen name="udfps_vertical_offset">10px</dimen>
</resources>
